  "_doc": "14 October 2026: the single parameter interface of the image (shader) measurement, HDA law. Every threshold of zrmd/shaders/field.py, zrmd/verify/imagescore.py and Scripts/ReproduceFieldSurvey.py lives here once. FR : interface unique de la mesure de l'image (shader), chaque seuil une seule fois.",
  "definition": [
    "The Image module (the shader chantier) judges the BACKDROP FIELD of every shot: the colour field, gradient and glow that a shader-bank composition of a few parameters reproduces, compared cell by cell with the reference.",
    "A frame pair is compared on a grid of grid.width x grid.height cells (area-averaged, a low pass at about 8 px of 1080p, R04 section 11.3), in CIEDE2000, one JND = jndDE.",
    "A cell is FIELD when its error is at most fieldCutoffDE (a fixed absolute cut, never a percentile of our own residual, so a bad fit cannot hide its errors); the other cells are CONTENT (text, UI, photograph: the vector chantier and the plate slots).",
    "Field fidelity of a frame = 1 - 0.01 x mean(dE00^2) over its field cells (R04 section 11.2: 0.99 means one JND of mean square error). Image value of a reference = mean of that over its field cells, weighted by shot duration and field share.",
    "Coverage of a reference = time-weighted share of cells that are field. within1Jnd = share of ALL cells at most one JND away (no mask at all, the pixel-honest number).",
    "Photographed plates stay animatics by design; they are reported (slot share) and never counted as failures. The 99.9 gate applies to the field fidelity; coverage and within1Jnd are shown beside it, never merged into it."
  ],
